# Git hooks are shell scripts and MUST check out with LF endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the Windows checkouts this repo runs from, which
# would otherwise give `.githooks/pre-push` a CRLF shebang. The kernel then
# reads the interpreter as `/bin/sh\r` and the hook fails with "bad
# interpreter" on macOS and Linux -- and a pre-push hook that cannot execute
# makes git ABORT THE PUSH rather than skip the hook.
#
# scripts/install-git-hooks.mjs also normalises to LF when it writes, so the
# guard survives a checkout that ignores this file. Both are deliberate: this
# rule fixes the working copy, the installer fixes what actually runs.
.githooks/** text eol=lf

# Prisma migrations MUST check out with LF endings, for a different reason.
#
# Prisma records each migration's checksum in production's _prisma_migrations as
# the sha256 of migration.sql AS IT SITS ON DISK. A CRLF working copy therefore
# records a checksum no Linux checkout of the same commit will ever match. Four
# production rows were written that way on 2026-10-03, each corrected by hand.
# scripts/prisma-migrate-deploy.cjs and scripts/prisma-resolve-prod.cjs refuse a
# CRLF checkout; this rule stops one from being created. Every committed
# migration.sql was already LF (205 of 205), so adding it renormalises nothing.
prisma/migrations/**/migration.sql text eol=lf
prisma/migrations-pending/**/migration.sql text eol=lf
